WEBVTT

02:52.540 --> 02:55.876
I'm sorry. Is this chair free?

02:58.612 --> 03:02.950
Yeah, um... sure.

03:12.793 --> 03:14.094
Thank you so much.

03:14.262 --> 03:15.796
You're welcome.

03:25.172 --> 03:27.441
-  Ah, whoo!

03:39.287 --> 03:41.755
And please don't give her any
apple juice before bedtime.

03:41.855 --> 03:43.791
Apple juice, yes, yes.
Like the other night.

03:43.891 --> 03:46.026
Yeah, but no apple juice.

03:46.126 --> 03:47.728
Yeah, it's too much sugar.

03:47.828 --> 03:48.929
Okay, no.

03:49.563 --> 03:50.798
- Hi-hi.
- Hi, Ma.

03:50.898 --> 03:52.300
- Ciao.
- Ciao.

03:52.400 --> 03:58.606
...cooking class.

04:01.475 --> 04:05.413
Today we made ravioli
with um,

04:05.513 --> 04:08.048
I think there were bits of
sausages inside it.

04:08.148 --> 04:10.418
Well, you should come
to the cooking class with us

04:10.518 --> 04:11.585
maybe tomorrow,

04:11.919 --> 04:14.422
because I believe that tomorrow
they're making the gnocchi.

04:14.922 --> 04:16.890
The ravioli that they tried to
teach--

04:16.990 --> 04:18.892
-  Oh, right.

04:20.193 --> 04:24.432
I'm sorry to bother you during
this very lovely dinner.

04:24.832 --> 04:29.703
I just want to say two things.
I hope we didn't wake you up,

04:29.803 --> 04:33.173
because the noise you heard last
night, the banging on the door,

04:33.341 --> 04:35.242
- Very quickly, that was me.

04:35.343 --> 04:36.944
- We couldn't find our way,

04:37.044 --> 04:38.579
so we were very late here.

04:38.679 --> 04:40.013
Ah-ah, sorry for that.

04:40.113 --> 04:42.015
Ah, we don't know each other.

04:42.483 --> 04:45.953
That's the way it goes on holidays.

04:46.053 --> 04:48.789
But uh, you know, I want to meet
you people,

04:48.889 --> 04:51.124
because you look all so nice
and beautiful.

04:51.224 --> 04:57.665
And uh, I want to toast to you,
guys. To Italy, of course.

04:57.765 --> 05:00.368
To the food, of course.
And to love.

05:00.434 --> 05:02.269
Too love, salute!

07:36.123 --> 07:40.360
Like a bunny... for kids?

07:41.895 --> 07:44.798
Nah? Okay, well. Ciao.

07:44.898 --> 07:45.799
Ciao.

08:13.460 --> 08:14.995
It goes up and down,
and up and down--

08:15.095 --> 08:17.598
It's so hot,
yeah. But you do it--

08:19.466 --> 08:22.069
Hi!
This is my husband, Bjørn.

08:22.169 --> 08:23.470
Patrick, nice to meet you.

08:23.571 --> 08:25.138
We met at the Villa?

08:26.574 --> 08:29.109
-  Hi.
- Hi. Karin.

08:29.209 --> 08:31.745
Sorry, I forgot to introduce
myself. I'm Louise--

08:31.845 --> 08:34.014
-  Hello.
- and this is Agnes.

08:34.381 --> 08:36.684
And what's your name?

08:39.587 --> 08:40.854
Abel has difficulties speaking.

08:40.954 --> 08:42.623
So, if he feels some sort
of pressure

08:42.723 --> 08:43.924
he can get
a little insecure.

08:44.024 --> 08:47.094
-  Ahh.
- But there's no pressure at all.

08:47.194 --> 08:48.161
And who is this?

08:49.496 --> 08:50.330
Ninus.

08:50.430 --> 08:51.498
Ninus?

08:51.832 --> 08:53.867
Agnes just lost it,
so Bjørn went to find it.

08:54.802 --> 08:56.770
You went to find the rabbit?

08:56.870 --> 08:57.838
Yes.

08:58.371 --> 08:59.840
That's very heroic of you.

09:01.141 --> 09:03.844
Thank you.

09:03.944 --> 09:06.614
No, no. I'm serious... respect.

09:08.115 --> 09:09.216
Well, thanks.

09:09.316 --> 09:10.618
You're very welcome.

09:11.484 --> 09:13.621
So, did you guys have lunch yet?

09:13.654 --> 09:15.623
By the way,
where are you guys from?

09:15.656 --> 09:16.957
Holland,
the southern part.

09:17.057 --> 09:18.726
Yeah, countryside,
it's a beautiful area.

09:18.826 --> 09:21.629
Wow, I would just love to move
outside the city

09:21.662 --> 09:24.264
and be close to nature and all--
yeah.

09:24.364 --> 09:25.866
Well, you should come and visit us.

09:25.966 --> 09:27.835
- That would be great--
-  Lasagna Vegeteriana.

09:27.935 --> 09:29.436
-  Prego.
- Ci , Vegetarian?

09:29.536 --> 09:30.771
-  Vegetarian.
- Yes, thank you.

09:30.871 --> 09:33.340
Tagliatelle ai funghi.
- Ci, grazia.

09:33.440 --> 09:35.075
E pizza margherita.

09:35.175 --> 09:36.644
So, you're a vegetarian?

09:36.744 --> 09:40.648
Yeah, I eat fish, but yes,
I'm a vegetarian.

09:40.681 --> 09:43.050
That's so good.
We could all learn from you.

09:43.550 --> 09:45.318
Yeah, good for the environment, really.

09:45.418 --> 09:46.353
Well... thank you--

09:46.453 --> 09:47.655
E peposo.

09:47.755 --> 09:49.422
Oh, Grazie mille .
Oh, I'm starving.

09:49.522 --> 09:50.991
- It looks good.
-  Looks great.

09:52.159 --> 09:53.026
Wow.

09:53.426 --> 09:56.964
Well, I actually think that
Dutch and Danish people

09:57.064 --> 09:58.231
are very similar.

09:58.331 --> 10:02.636
Yeah, so we're the same.

10:02.736 --> 10:06.239
Well, in many ways I think so, actually.

10:06.339 --> 10:08.175
It's uh, the same humor,

10:08.275 --> 10:11.311
the same um, the same um...
same culture.

10:11.411 --> 10:15.548
Yeah, at least we have more in
common with people from Holland,

10:15.649 --> 10:17.417
than with the Swedish people.

10:17.517 --> 10:19.386
I's so glad you say that.

10:19.486 --> 10:20.487
- Yeah?

10:20.721 --> 10:22.355
Really. No, I had
a Swedish colleague

10:22.455 --> 10:25.592
when I worked for the Médecins
Sans Frontières.

10:25.693 --> 10:26.526
You're a doctor?

10:26.626 --> 10:27.695
Yeah.

10:28.195 --> 10:30.731
No, really. He was the most
boring and political correct man

10:30.831 --> 10:32.666
I've ever met in my entire life.

10:32.766 --> 10:33.834
-  Really.

10:40.140 --> 10:42.943
...you know saying weird
stuff!

10:43.510 --> 10:49.182
Like once we were in Greece,
I was going with the cheering.

10:49.282 --> 10:51.785
I was going... "Kalimera!"

10:53.586 --> 10:54.688
Good morning!

12:35.322 --> 12:39.827
"Dear Louise, Bjørn and Agnes.
How are you?

12:39.860 --> 12:42.195
We were just talking
the other day

12:42.295 --> 12:45.665
how nice it was spending time
with you this summer.

12:46.299 --> 12:50.003
And even though
it's been a while,

12:50.103 --> 12:53.006
we would love to invite you
to come to visit us.

12:53.106 --> 12:56.376
- What do you say?"

12:56.476 --> 13:00.447
"A weekend
in the Dutch countryside.

13:00.547 --> 13:03.516
Food, wine and long walks.

13:04.684 --> 13:09.756
And, oh, by the way, Abel keeps
mentioning Agnes. So funny.

13:09.857 --> 13:11.458
He really misses her.

13:11.558 --> 13:15.195
All the best
from Abel, Patrick and Karin."

17:36.389 --> 17:38.125
Yeah, you made it!

17:38.225 --> 17:39.159
Finally, yes.

17:39.259 --> 17:41.128
Yes, yes!

17:41.461 --> 17:43.663
-  Hi.

17:47.134 --> 17:49.169
So nice
to see you again.

17:49.269 --> 17:50.337
Hey, man.

17:50.437 --> 17:52.004
What a beautiful place.

17:52.139 --> 17:53.039
Thank you.

17:53.740 --> 17:57.444
Oh no, you can leave
them on. Or take them off.

17:57.544 --> 17:58.411
Leave them on.

17:58.511 --> 17:59.512
Or take them off.

17:59.912 --> 18:01.414
Leaving 'em on, taking 'em off,
whatever you want.

18:01.514 --> 18:02.715
- Thank you.

18:02.815 --> 18:04.584
- Give me your coat.
- Thank you.

18:04.684 --> 18:05.618
Sorry for the mess.

18:05.718 --> 18:06.819
Oh, it's nothing.

18:06.919 --> 18:08.955
It's gonna get much worse. Come
on!

18:10.157 --> 18:11.023
So, come in.

18:11.391 --> 18:14.261
Wow, very comfortable.

18:14.361 --> 18:16.529
Yeah, that's the way we like it.

18:16.629 --> 18:17.897
Oh, and we brought you something.

18:17.997 --> 18:18.831
Oh!

18:19.031 --> 18:20.633
It's a little souvenir
from Denmark.

18:20.733 --> 18:22.402
It's Louise who bought
it, so...

18:22.502 --> 18:23.836
Thank you.

18:24.471 --> 18:25.705
Uh, where's Abel?

18:25.805 --> 18:27.574
- Uh, downstairs maybe?
- Oh.

18:27.674 --> 18:30.042
He's been cooking all day.
He's making Wild Boar.

18:31.511 --> 18:33.446
Come on.
This is your room.

18:33.846 --> 18:36.449
- Wow.
- Ah, that's wonderful.

18:38.551 --> 18:39.919
-  Bjørn?
- Yes.

18:40.019 --> 18:41.421
- You want a beer?
-  Yeah.

18:41.521 --> 18:42.755
I want to show you my pool.

18:43.190 --> 18:44.424
- You have a pool?
-  Uh-huh.

18:51.964 --> 18:52.899
Hi Abel.

18:59.105 --> 19:02.041
Look, Agnes, we made you a
little bed.

19:05.745 --> 19:08.114
-  Do you like it?
- Yes, she likes it.

19:11.918 --> 19:14.787
I forgot the presents.
I'm so sorry.

19:14.887 --> 19:16.656
No, it's fine.

19:18.791 --> 19:24.331
Wow... it's coffee cups.
That's sweet.

19:24.431 --> 19:26.566
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

19:26.666 --> 19:30.002
And... a mermaid?

19:30.102 --> 19:34.741
Yes, it's something that I think
represents Denmark very well.

19:34.841 --> 19:36.543
- It's The Little Mermaid.
- Yeah.

19:36.643 --> 19:37.544
I know it.

19:38.010 --> 19:40.380
I've heard it's quite small
and disappointing.

19:41.881 --> 19:43.850
Well, actually there are some
anecdotes about it

19:43.950 --> 19:45.051
that are really nice.

19:45.151 --> 19:47.920
Oh yeah, you know what is also
nice?

19:48.621 --> 19:50.290
- Louise...
- Hmm?

19:52.359 --> 19:53.593
This is for you.

19:53.693 --> 19:55.262
Oh, no-no, that's fine--

19:55.362 --> 19:56.529
I insist.

19:56.629 --> 19:58.565
- I insist.

19:58.665 --> 20:00.400
No-no,
I'll wait till--

20:00.800 --> 20:02.569
- It's my favorite part.
- Okay.

20:02.669 --> 20:05.204
It's delicious. It's crispy and
soft at the same time.

20:05.305 --> 20:07.940
- Yes.

20:08.475 --> 20:09.376
Yeah.

20:14.614 --> 20:16.115
- Hmm.
- It's good, right?

20:16.215 --> 20:17.484
Very good.

21:04.331 --> 21:05.932
Oh, hi Abel.

21:44.070 --> 21:46.506
But it is really lucky we've got
the GPS,

21:46.606 --> 21:49.542
because otherwise we'd have got
lost like 20 times

21:49.642 --> 21:50.743
I had it under control.

21:50.843 --> 21:52.845
No, [laughing] the GPS had.

21:52.945 --> 21:54.714
- I had.

21:58.685 --> 22:00.420
It's frightening sometimes,

22:00.520 --> 22:03.623
how we lose our ability to find
our way through life.

22:03.723 --> 22:07.427
Because we hand over the
responsibility to technology.

22:07.527 --> 22:08.828
That is so true.

22:08.961 --> 22:11.664
I mean, people nowadays don't
have a clue how to read a map.

22:13.132 --> 22:17.404
I must admit that driving in a
car like that,

22:17.470 --> 22:22.509
with GPS and all these
modern things, you--

22:23.209 --> 22:26.278
I-I want to turn it off sometimes.

22:26.879 --> 22:28.147
And, as you were saying,
Patrick--

22:28.247 --> 22:29.716
Is he all right?

22:29.849 --> 22:35.054
No, no, he's fine. He's fine.
He'll fall asleep in a minute.

22:36.423 --> 22:40.192
He just does this sometimes.
It's part of his disease.

22:40.292 --> 22:42.094
Oh yeah, what is that?

22:42.194 --> 22:44.864
Abel has what you call
"congenital aglossia".

22:45.432 --> 22:48.535
Meaning basically, he's born
without a tongue.

22:48.635 --> 22:52.304
Or... a much smaller tongue than
you and me.

22:52.705 --> 22:53.673
But is he in pain?

22:53.773 --> 22:54.941
Oh no, no pain.

22:55.575 --> 22:58.177
He just has a hard time
making himself understandable.

22:58.645 --> 23:01.681
Oh no, I understand everything
he says.

24:30.837 --> 24:32.939
Excuse me
for just one second.

24:38.244 --> 24:41.614
Um, Abel, do you think you could
move away?

24:41.714 --> 24:44.984
Uh, because Agnes really wants
to try it.

24:58.565 --> 24:59.999
Uh, excuse me?

25:01.033 --> 25:03.102
Agnes really wants
to try the slide.

25:03.202 --> 25:04.837
And do you think
it is possible

25:04.937 --> 25:08.708
to ask Abel to move away
just for one second?

25:13.379 --> 25:15.214
So sorry about this.

25:15.314 --> 25:17.483
No, it's okay, it's nothing.

25:23.823 --> 25:25.925
Patrick, it's all right.
He doesn't have to.

25:26.025 --> 25:28.360
No, he wants to say
"I apologize".

25:28.460 --> 25:30.496
Yeah,
he really wants to.

25:32.298 --> 25:33.600
Sorry.

25:44.811 --> 25:45.978
- I must have the recipe.
- It's good, right?

25:46.078 --> 25:48.715
It reminds me
of what we call a Mazarin?

25:48.815 --> 25:52.785
A Mazarin tart...
a Danish thing.

25:53.319 --> 25:54.621
Come here.

26:14.473 --> 26:16.643
Hey, am I interrupting?

26:16.676 --> 26:18.177
No-no, of course not.

26:18.277 --> 26:21.513
Well Patrick and I would like to
invite you to dinner tonight.

26:21.648 --> 26:23.883
Oh, that's so nice of you.

26:23.983 --> 26:26.485
Yeah, there's a nice restaurant
with great local food

26:26.653 --> 26:27.654
just up the road.

26:27.920 --> 26:29.989
And we wouldn't want you
to miss the opportunity

26:30.089 --> 26:30.723
while you're here.

26:30.823 --> 26:32.091
That sounds good.

26:32.191 --> 26:33.225
Great.

27:00.419 --> 27:03.222
Yes, perfect timing.

27:23.542 --> 27:25.277
He doesn't speak
any English.

27:25.377 --> 27:26.412
And who is Muhajid?

27:26.512 --> 27:28.047
He's the babysitter.

27:28.948 --> 27:30.349
- The babysitter?
-  Yeah.

27:35.554 --> 27:37.824
But the kids are going as well, right?

27:37.924 --> 27:41.327
No, tonight is without kids.
Didn't I tell you that?

27:46.198 --> 27:48.000
Muhajid is so very good
with children.

27:48.100 --> 27:51.170
The whole neighborhood uses him
and not only because he's cheap.

27:55.842 --> 27:57.276
Let's go!

27:59.645 --> 28:01.080
Come on, let's move.

28:24.937 --> 28:27.139
Patrick, are we at the
restaurant soon?

28:27.573 --> 28:29.108
We'll be there in a minute.

28:38.918 --> 28:41.353
Uh, What is the "stamppot"?

28:41.453 --> 28:45.958
Oh, that's great. It's the house
specialty... you should try it,

28:46.425 --> 28:47.159
- Okay
- It's good.

28:47.259 --> 28:49.528
Yeah, and the "boerenkool"?

28:49.628 --> 28:52.965
Boerenkool. Oh, that's also
stamppot, you'll love it.

28:53.065 --> 28:55.201
It's delicious, they make it
very well here.

28:56.702 --> 28:58.470
And what is stamppot?

28:58.570 --> 29:02.041
Stamppot? Oh, that's typical
Dutch. Very traditional.

29:02.141 --> 29:05.111
Like potatoes and vegetables,
you stamp it all together.

29:05.211 --> 29:08.114
Steef! Let me take care of you
guys. Okay?

29:08.214 --> 29:09.882
Yeah, fine with me.

29:17.924 --> 29:20.226
And remember, I'm a vegetarian.

29:20.326 --> 29:20.993
I'm sorry?

29:21.093 --> 29:22.161
Yes, I don't eat meat.

29:22.494 --> 29:24.663
Oh, yes, yes. So good
for the environment, yes.

29:24.831 --> 29:26.332
But you eat fish, right?

29:26.432 --> 29:27.266
Yes.

29:27.699 --> 29:29.601
So you're not a vegetarian,
you're a pescatarian.

29:30.469 --> 29:31.303
Yes.

29:31.403 --> 29:32.504
Yes, Steef?

29:37.409 --> 29:38.477
Hmm?

29:39.979 --> 29:42.148
And fish is not meat?

29:42.248 --> 29:46.052
Of course, um, but it's better
for the environment.

29:47.286 --> 29:49.121
And the way
the fishing industry works

29:49.221 --> 29:52.491
and how we treat the oceans
is not affecting the climate?

29:58.630 --> 30:01.067
Well, I would like
to propose a toast--

30:01.167 --> 30:02.101
- Okay.
- For uh,

30:02.201 --> 30:04.136
- good times.
- For good times.

30:04.236 --> 30:06.105
- We say proost.

30:06.205 --> 30:07.439
- Proost.
- Proost.

30:07.539 --> 30:09.408
-  Proost.

30:15.882 --> 30:17.083
Well,
I just hate this...

30:19.518 --> 30:24.623
This, um, this team building
bullshit, you know.

30:42.474 --> 30:46.245
♪ Was just in time replaced
By the magic appearance ♪

30:46.345 --> 30:47.846
Of a new day while ♪

30:47.947 --> 30:51.717
♪ A melancholic reno was
crawling on his back just in ♪

30:51.817 --> 30:54.420
♪ Front of
The supermarket doorway ♪

30:57.689 --> 31:02.929
♪ On a cold summer night as we
stood on the corner ♪

31:02.962 --> 31:05.597
♪ As a man passed by and asked
us what we were doing ♪

31:05.697 --> 31:06.498
What we need ♪

31:07.766 --> 31:10.836
♪ As he pointed
His big fat finger ♪

31:10.937 --> 31:12.638
♪ To the people hangin' round ♪

31:12.738 --> 31:16.108
♪ At the corner
Of the other side of street ♪

31:16.208 --> 31:17.576
Oh well ♪

31:19.211 --> 31:22.514
♪ Doin' nothing,
just hanging around... ♪

31:29.155 --> 31:33.993
♪ Doin' nothing,
just hanging around ♪

31:34.093 --> 31:39.831
♪ His head all busted lookin'
just a little too wise child ♪

31:39.966 --> 31:41.867
I just can't wait ♪

31:44.536 --> 31:46.472
I just can't wait ♪

31:48.540 --> 31:50.542
For Saturday night ♪

31:53.879 --> 31:56.282
For Saturday night ♪

31:59.051 --> 32:01.487
For Saturday night ♪

32:04.290 --> 32:06.658
Saturday night ♪

32:14.633 --> 32:16.635
Saturday night ♪

32:20.072 --> 32:21.573
Saturday night. ♪

32:21.673 --> 32:22.674
Wow.

32:23.309 --> 32:26.312
Someone had
a really good time tonight.

32:26.412 --> 32:27.646
You want us to chip in?

32:27.746 --> 32:29.481
Oh, thanks man.

32:39.491 --> 32:42.094
So the dinner is on us?

32:42.761 --> 32:46.165
Oh, that's so kind.
Thanks, man, thanks.

32:56.675 --> 32:57.909
Ah.

33:27.539 --> 33:30.476
Patrick, can you turn down the
music a bit?

33:34.080 --> 33:35.947
Patrick, the music, can you turn
it down--

33:36.082 --> 33:39.685
I love this song.
This is a great song!

33:39.785 --> 33:42.088
Turn down the fucking music.

33:43.089 --> 33:44.556
Listen to it!

33:52.964 --> 33:58.504
I'm so sorry, he's just so
drunk. I'm truly sorry. Okay?

34:00.406 --> 34:03.642
I truly apologize,
I'm so sorry.

34:05.010 --> 34:06.378
And ya!

34:09.815 --> 34:12.818
- Patrick!
- Just a little bit, please?

34:13.252 --> 34:14.820
Just a little bit down.

34:19.991 --> 34:21.760
-  Okay, a little bit.
- Yeah!

34:23.129 --> 34:24.996
Yeah. Thank you.

39:21.760 --> 39:29.167
Bjørn, Bjorn, Bjørn, Bjorn!

39:30.001 --> 39:30.902
Bjørn.

43:46.124 --> 43:49.928
We had
some really lovely days here.

43:50.028 --> 43:52.430
- Huh?
-  What's going on?

43:52.530 --> 43:55.701
Well, uh,
we have a situation here.

43:55.767 --> 43:59.004
Someone left
without saying goodbye.

43:59.104 --> 44:01.472
No, as I was just trying
to tell Patrick,

44:01.572 --> 44:03.875
we had some really lovely days.

44:03.975 --> 44:05.744
And then I ask again, why are
you leaving--

44:07.813 --> 44:10.849
We had some good days,
it's just um...

44:12.951 --> 44:16.454
there's just some things that...

44:17.188 --> 44:21.226
that make us believe that
it's best that we go home.

44:21.727 --> 44:23.729
What are those things?
I want to know.

44:23.762 --> 44:26.732
- It's um, many things.
- Such as?

44:31.002 --> 44:34.039
It's just, um... such as...

44:36.507 --> 44:40.011
Such as the bed for instance.
It's really small, and uh,

44:40.478 --> 44:44.783
and Agnes doesn't want to sleep
on the floor,

44:44.883 --> 44:47.385
so she comes in at night.

44:52.290 --> 44:58.764
Okay, so
with all of your respect...

45:00.131 --> 45:03.168
First of all, I'm a vegetarian.

45:03.268 --> 45:07.438
But all you've been doing since
we got here was serving meat.

45:07.538 --> 45:10.108
But we have all sorts of food.
You can have a hagelslag

45:10.208 --> 45:11.676
sandwich right now.
I can make it for you.

45:11.777 --> 45:13.812
No, thank you.

45:13.912 --> 45:17.916
And last night
at that restaurant or...

45:18.316 --> 45:21.987
roadhouse or whatever that place
was, it was...

45:22.821 --> 45:26.124
it was very uncomfortable
to drive.

45:27.525 --> 45:30.361
And the music was so loud.

45:31.797 --> 45:34.532
And you were drinking
and driving.

45:36.534 --> 45:41.306
And the way you were touching
each other in front of us

45:41.406 --> 45:44.709
that just made me so
uncomfortable, I'm really sorry.

45:45.510 --> 45:50.615
But it just um... so many things
have felt so wrong.

45:51.516 --> 45:54.285
I'm really sorry,
but it's just how it is.

46:06.832 --> 46:08.566
I'm in shock.

46:16.607 --> 46:18.944
Can-can I say something?

46:22.747 --> 46:26.184
Uh, first of all... Louise.

46:26.284 --> 46:31.256
I am so sorry that we forgot
that you were a vegetarian.

46:32.023 --> 46:35.193
And if there are things
you don't eat,

46:35.293 --> 46:38.029
you just could have told us.

46:39.264 --> 46:39.898
Right?

46:40.966 --> 46:43.068
And our house is not huge,

46:43.168 --> 46:46.404
so we cannot offer you
a big luxury room

46:46.504 --> 46:49.640
and a king-size bed, Bjørn.
I'm sorry.

46:49.740 --> 46:53.711
And I am truly sorry that Agnes
doesn't feel comfortable

46:53.879 --> 46:57.883
staying in Abel's room. But we
thought it was only natural.

46:57.949 --> 47:01.953
I mean, if you only knew how
much Abel was looking forward to

47:02.053 --> 47:05.256
sharing his toys
in his room with Agnes.

47:05.356 --> 47:09.394
And the roadhouse,
as you call it...

47:10.028 --> 47:13.464
the hugging and the dancing.

47:15.566 --> 47:19.470
We were just having a fun
evening. Guys, come on.

47:19.570 --> 47:23.975
I mean, dancing
and kissing the one you love.

47:24.075 --> 47:25.911
What's the problem?

47:26.011 --> 47:27.412
To me, it's crossing the line

47:27.512 --> 47:29.780
when you pick up my daughter
at night.

47:30.448 --> 47:32.383
And then you take her
into your bed,

47:32.483 --> 47:34.685
where you slept next to her, naked.

47:37.055 --> 47:39.925
Yeah but, where were you?

47:39.958 --> 47:44.162
Louise,
I mean, Agnes kept calling?

47:44.762 --> 47:46.797
She was crying.

47:51.169 --> 47:52.637
Where were you?

47:56.507 --> 47:59.444
First of all there's nothing we
can do now to change the way

47:59.544 --> 48:02.047
you have felt
during these past few days.

48:02.413 --> 48:04.082
And it truly breaks my heart
to hear

48:04.182 --> 48:05.850
that you haven't enjoyed
your stay.

48:06.251 --> 48:08.719
It makes me wonder
if maybe I've failed as a host.

48:10.321 --> 48:12.390
No one is forcing you to stay.

48:13.524 --> 48:18.396
But I really hope you do, 'cause
today is gonna be a great day.

48:18.763 --> 48:22.667
I promise you, today,
it's gonna be great.

48:43.188 --> 48:47.025
It's this scissor. It doesn't
cut anything, it's so dull.

49:08.913 --> 49:11.182
This is okay
if I turn on the radio?

49:11.282 --> 49:13.351
Yeah, of course.

49:17.455 --> 49:19.524
You can turn it up if you like.

49:28.566 --> 49:31.369
So, what kind of music
do you like?

49:31.936 --> 49:32.837
Ah, well...

49:33.904 --> 49:38.376
yeah, I listen to,
you know, all kinds.

49:38.476 --> 49:42.513
Like uh... like pop
and rock and, uh...

49:43.281 --> 49:46.084
yeah, basically all kinds
you know.

49:46.184 --> 49:47.852
- And you?
- Me too.

49:48.586 --> 49:51.089
Pop, rock... funk.

49:51.656 --> 49:52.457
Hmm.

49:53.124 --> 49:56.661
I like music that I can sing
along to. I like singing.

49:57.362 --> 49:59.664
- Yeah, singing is good.
- Yeah.

50:00.398 --> 50:03.268
Actually, there's a lot
of great Dutch music.

50:03.368 --> 50:05.303
You want me
to play you some?

50:05.770 --> 50:08.673
Yeah yeah, please. I'd really
like to hear some.

50:08.773 --> 50:11.109
- You sure?
- Yeah, really.

50:20.085 --> 50:22.053
This is called "It Never Ends".

50:40.605 --> 50:42.240
And who is it?

50:42.340 --> 50:43.774
Trijntje Oosterhuis.

50:44.509 --> 50:47.178
I think,
this is how an angel sounds.

50:59.890 --> 51:02.093
I really want to apologize
for my behavior last night.

51:02.660 --> 51:06.264
I'm sorry I made you feel
so uncomfortable.

51:06.364 --> 51:10.135
No, it's fine.
Don't worry about it.

51:12.803 --> 51:18.042
You know, sometimes I have
this thing, right here.

51:19.810 --> 51:23.013
And it's so powerful and wild.

51:23.714 --> 51:27.252
And I like it.
That's the weird part.

51:27.352 --> 51:30.355
I really like it.
You understand?

51:30.455 --> 51:31.822
Yeah.

51:32.290 --> 51:33.691
You do?

51:34.159 --> 51:35.293
Totally.

51:38.596 --> 51:40.931
Normally, I just uh...

51:42.400 --> 51:44.835
just try to hold it down or...

51:45.503 --> 51:47.905
keep it in chains.

51:48.939 --> 51:50.175
Why?

51:50.775 --> 51:53.878
I don't know why.

51:56.547 --> 51:58.316
Too many rules, I guess...

51:59.584 --> 52:01.686
- It's um--
- It's what?

52:04.422 --> 52:06.090
It's clau--
Yeah, I don't know,

52:06.191 --> 52:10.195
It's... claustrophobic,
you know?

52:12.197 --> 52:15.233
It's like I become this person
I don't want to be.

52:18.769 --> 52:20.305
Who is that person?

52:22.006 --> 52:26.744
I don't know. It's... some guy.

52:28.213 --> 52:31.216
Some normal guy who gets up
in the morning and...

52:31.282 --> 52:36.221
... takes his daughter
to school and... goes to work.

52:39.224 --> 52:43.661
Play a little squash
once a week.

52:46.063 --> 52:49.300
Have dinner with people
I don't even like.

53:00.545 --> 53:02.880
And I'm so tired
of smiling all the time.

53:10.688 --> 53:12.257
Come.

53:14.091 --> 53:17.027
Come, I want
to show you something.

54:28.366 --> 54:31.736
- It's fantastic.
- This is the life, huh?

54:40.678 --> 54:43.648
Louise, thank you so much
for helping out in the garden.

54:43.748 --> 54:45.149
Oh, you're very welcome.

54:51.188 --> 54:53.358
Um, they want to show a dance.

54:53.391 --> 54:57.462
Oh, that's so nice. Maybe when
we have coffee.

55:00.030 --> 55:03.634
Agnes, can you set the table, please?

55:11.409 --> 55:12.610
Ah!

55:18.616 --> 55:21.386
Patrick, maybe you could take a
look at her finger?

55:22.720 --> 55:24.254
Sure.

55:30.728 --> 55:32.697
It's good that we have a doctor
in the house.

55:32.797 --> 55:34.131
I'm not a doctor.

55:35.733 --> 55:38.703
But didn't you say
you were a doctor?

55:38.803 --> 55:40.838
Did I? Oh, I lied.

55:40.938 --> 55:42.540
- You lied?
-  Yeah.

55:42.640 --> 55:45.242
Sometimes I get a little
insecure when I meet new people.

55:45.410 --> 55:47.512
He just wanted to make a good impression.

55:54.251 --> 55:55.920
What do you work with then?

55:56.020 --> 55:57.855
- I don't work.
- No?

55:57.955 --> 55:59.089
No, I'm unemployed.

55:59.323 --> 56:01.426
I've never worked,
I don't believe in working.

56:03.494 --> 56:04.529
Uh.

56:05.496 --> 56:09.434
Oh, that's wrong. It's the other
way around.

56:17.307 --> 56:18.443
Okay?

56:18.476 --> 56:19.844
Sorry.

56:19.944 --> 56:21.446
-  Yes.
- No, ow! Okay.

56:22.046 --> 56:24.214
Yeah, I got this, thank you.

56:25.015 --> 56:26.451
Who needs a doctor, right?

56:30.020 --> 56:33.223
Bread? Yes.

56:35.460 --> 56:37.194
You know, it's a shame

56:37.294 --> 56:41.098
that Holland is not really
being recognized

56:41.198 --> 56:43.333
as a producer of fine
and high quality cheese

56:43.468 --> 56:46.170
like Italy or France
for example.

56:46.270 --> 56:48.205
Oh, here.

56:48.305 --> 56:50.541
I mean, we are a cheese nation.

56:50.641 --> 56:53.243
We export more cheese than any
other country in the world,

56:53.343 --> 56:55.145
besides Germany, of course.

56:55.245 --> 56:56.481
But I sometimes feel...

56:56.981 --> 57:00.317
that Dutch cheese is not getting
the respect it deserves.

57:14.398 --> 57:17.367
Everyone should come with Bjørn
and me to the market

57:17.502 --> 57:19.403
and try some of Johan's cheese.

57:19.504 --> 57:22.507
Then they will give Dutch cheese
the respect it deserves.

57:22.840 --> 57:24.008
Johan said it himself.

57:24.108 --> 57:25.843
Forget Stilton,
forget Gorgonzola.

57:25.943 --> 57:29.346
Dutch cheese, Dutch cheese
is the number one, right?

57:29.514 --> 57:30.548
- Bjørn.
- Hmm?

57:30.815 --> 57:32.316
The cheese at the market,
it was good, right?

57:32.416 --> 57:34.919
- It was fantastic.
- It was number one.

57:35.019 --> 57:37.622
- Johan said it himself, cheers!

57:37.722 --> 57:40.691
- Cheers.

57:46.697 --> 57:48.866
Stop telling my daughter what
to do.

57:52.970 --> 57:56.440
It's not up to you to tell
my daughter what to do, okay?

57:57.007 --> 58:00.545
Okay, relax. I'm sorry.

58:36.714 --> 58:37.815
Sorry about that.

58:37.915 --> 58:39.650
-  Okay?

58:40.450 --> 58:44.421
One, two, three, four.

58:54.331 --> 58:56.233
It's okay.
They're both really good.

58:56.333 --> 58:59.770
Yes, but he has no rhythm.
And he's messing up the routine.

58:59.870 --> 59:01.706
No, but they are just kids.

59:01.806 --> 59:04.274
Yes, but if he wants to reach
his potential,

59:04.374 --> 59:06.343
he has to concentrate,
right? Right.

59:09.647 --> 59:12.817
Okay, one more time.

59:39.777 --> 59:42.012
No, she has to stay
because it's a duet.

59:42.112 --> 59:43.447
No,
she doesn't want to.

59:43.547 --> 59:44.649
No, she has to stay.

59:44.682 --> 59:46.216
She doesn't want to dance anymore.

01:00:57.855 --> 01:00:59.957
Uh, what's the problem?

01:01:02.092 --> 01:01:06.163
You cannot... he's only a child
for Christ's sake.

01:01:07.131 --> 01:01:12.602
I mean, what the hell is wrong
with you?

01:01:12.737 --> 01:01:15.940
Can't you see he's crying?
He's in pain?

01:01:17.908 --> 01:01:20.444
You can't talk to him that way.
What is wrong with you?

01:01:20.544 --> 01:01:23.347
Oh my god, what's wrong?

01:01:23.748 --> 01:01:26.183
Because we do things
differently?

01:01:26.283 --> 01:01:29.253
This is not about doing things differently.

01:01:29.353 --> 01:01:30.620
It's not about that.

01:01:30.988 --> 01:01:33.323
No! This is about doing
what is right.

01:01:33.423 --> 01:01:37.762
This is really...
to do what is right for you.

01:01:37.795 --> 01:01:39.463
Like showing your son some love
when he is crying

01:01:39.563 --> 01:01:41.031
instead of shouting
at him.

01:01:41.131 --> 01:01:42.767
Yeah, and Patrick,
what the fuck?

01:01:42.867 --> 01:01:44.769
Why can't you just
let him dance?

01:01:45.535 --> 01:01:47.204
Oh, that wasn't dancing.

01:01:48.906 --> 01:01:49.940
Yeah, but you threw a cup
at him!

01:01:51.508 --> 01:01:53.043
Sorry, but I can't listen to you
talk to him that way.

01:01:54.411 --> 01:01:55.980
You threw a cup at the wall!

01:01:59.784 --> 01:02:01.952
Okay, stop this please.
Please stop it.

01:02:35.820 --> 01:02:37.087
Bjørn, can you please
take her inside?

01:02:37.187 --> 01:02:39.123
I don't want her to see me
like this.

01:14:27.263 --> 01:14:28.532
Hello?

01:14:41.410 --> 01:14:42.746
Hello!?

01:14:47.383 --> 01:14:48.585
Hello!?

01:15:02.065 --> 01:15:03.099
Louise?

01:15:07.837 --> 01:15:09.072
Louise!?

01:15:13.242 --> 01:15:14.443
Louise!?

01:15:22.586 --> 01:15:23.953
Agnes!?

01:15:28.191 --> 01:15:29.593
Agnes!?

01:15:38.434 --> 01:15:40.103
Louise!?

01:15:53.449 --> 01:15:56.485
Agnes!

01:16:26.282 --> 01:16:27.183
Hey Bjørn.

01:16:34.691 --> 01:16:35.892
Thanks for the call.

01:16:37.994 --> 01:16:41.030
I'm glad you agreed
to meet us up on the road.

01:16:41.931 --> 01:16:46.035
Thanks for helping us out.
It's very nice of you.

01:16:46.135 --> 01:16:47.671
Of course, hmm.

01:17:04.688 --> 01:17:05.521
Get in the car.

01:17:06.489 --> 01:17:11.260
Please don't hurt
us. Please don't hurt my family.

01:17:12.862 --> 01:17:14.330
We just want to go home.

01:17:17.400 --> 01:17:21.370
Hey, it's okay. Relax.

01:17:21.738 --> 01:17:25.274
As long as you do as we say,
it's gonna be fine.

01:17:41.090 --> 01:17:43.426
Do you know when we
will be back at the house?

01:17:43.893 --> 01:17:45.795
It won't be long now.

01:18:00.176 --> 01:18:01.878
Is Abel alone
at the house?

01:18:01.978 --> 01:18:04.080
No, Muhajid is looking
after him.

01:18:05.014 --> 01:18:08.151
He was up early anyway, so...

01:19:36.105 --> 01:19:37.440
Are we there soon?

01:19:45.849 --> 01:19:47.250
Be quiet.

01:19:50.019 --> 01:19:51.654
Excuse me?

01:19:56.860 --> 01:19:58.962
Will you be quiet, please?

01:20:04.633 --> 01:20:06.903
Can you tell us when
we'll be back at the house?

01:20:07.003 --> 01:20:09.238
Shhhhhh.

01:20:17.346 --> 01:20:19.448
We're going
to your house, right?

01:21:14.170 --> 01:21:15.638
Now you have to tell us
what's going on--

01:21:15.738 --> 01:21:17.506
Shut up. Shut the fuck up.

01:21:17.606 --> 01:21:19.943
- Don't talk to my family like--

01:21:52.976 --> 01:21:56.279
Louise, please let go of her.

01:22:06.389 --> 01:22:07.590
Louise...

01:22:10.059 --> 01:22:11.427
You will let go, yes.

01:22:11.527 --> 01:22:13.896
- No.
-  You will, you will.

01:25:55.618 --> 01:25:57.686
Why are you doing this?

01:26:01.890 --> 01:26:03.426
Because you let me.

01:26:15.538 --> 01:26:17.273
Take off your clothes.
